## Requirements *(mandatory)*

### User Story 5 - Standardized Null Handling (Priority: P3)

<!--

As a developer, when I work with data that might be null or empty, I should have consistent helper methods that prevent null reference exceptions and ensure predictable behavior across all forms.  ACTION REQUIRED: The content in this section represents placeholders.

  Fill them out with the right functional requirements.

**Why this priority**: Null reference exceptions are a common source of crashes. Standardizing null handling prevents these errors proactively.-->



**Independent Test**: Can be fully tested by code review identifying all places where null checks are needed and verifying they use standardized helper methods, plus testing with null/empty data scenarios.### Constitution Compliance Check *(KPP-specific)*



**Acceptance Scenarios**:Before proceeding, verify this feature aligns with project constitution:



1. **Given** a form retrieves data from the database, **When** a field might be null, **Then** the code uses null-coalescing operators or helper methods to provide safe defaults- [ ] **Stability First**: Does not degrade existing production functionality

2. **Given** a user doesn't enter data in an optional field, **When** the form processes the data, **Then** no null reference exception occurs- [ ] **Backward Compatibility**: Preserves legacy data and workflows

3. **Given** a dropdown has no selection, **When** the form accesses the selected value, **Then** the code safely handles the null case- [ ] **Data Integrity**: Maintains audit trails (korisnikId, azurirano fields)

4. **Given** autocomplete suggestions might be empty, **When** displaying the list, **Then** the code handles empty collections gracefully- [ ] **Validation Culture**: Required field validation with pink highlight feedback

- [ ] **Security**: Respects role-based permissions (Administrator/User)

---- [ ] **Code Quality**: Follows MVC pattern and uses helper classes

- [ ] **Consistent UX**: Uses standard form layout (DataGridView + search/filter + CRUD buttons)

